In window mode the launcher prints its startup lines (cmd/launcher/main.go ~:73-91: config load, engine resolution, the EngineAssociation WARN from k88, other info.Warnings) to the console before it switches output to unreagent.log. Those lines go to the console only and are missing from the log, so a user who reads unreagent.log after a window-mode start does not see why a fallback engine was chosen.

Done when: the lines printed before the switch also land in unreagent.log (buffered and replayed after the log opens, or the log opened earlier, as long as a failed MCP bind still writes no file — k123), with a test that pins it. Found during the k45/k88 review.

Main agent's decision 2026-11-21: k150, k151 and k152 go to one unreagent-worker as a bundle, since all three are about what reaches the console and the log. The cards stay separate.
- **k150:** buffer the lines printed before the log switch, and replay them into unreagent.log once it opens. Keep their original timestamps. A failed MCP bind still writes no file (k123).
- **k151:** in window mode, the supervisor's own lines and the console-command outcomes (started, stopped, restarted, leave, shutdown) go to the console as well as to the log.
- **k152:** each failed agent start that the restart policy retries leaves exactly one console line naming the error and the retry. When the policy gives up, the existing 'Agent did not start' prompt stays as it is.

